※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=7 diag=none

※ A type that is not a type parameter has no apostrophe to mark it, so it is
※ written between the lifting marks -- which is what the marks are for
※ everywhere else, and is the fourth place that reads one.
※
※ A bundle applied to a concrete type is how a program asks whether that type
※ is one of whatever the bundle names.

bundle number(T'):  T' ⊞ T' → T'

fn total(a: T', b: T') → T' pre(number(⌜u8⌝)) pre(T' ⊞ T' → T'):
    a ⊞ b

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(total(3u8, 4u8), ⌜u6⌝) ?? 1u6
